# One release per line: a `key=value ...` context for `req gate`. The reader is
# `scripts/check.sh` (and any CI that runs it) — req itself knows nothing about this file, so
# the format is the reader's: `#` starts a comment, and a line that is empty after stripping it
# is skipped.
#
# Two releases, not one, and the corpus says why: `corpus_set` takes two mutually exclusive
# values, so no single context can apply both REQ-0008 (parity and adversarial) and REQ-0010
# (parity). Every *other* scoped claim must be decided in both, or `dependencies_decided`
# refuses to answer rather than skipping — measured: a context carrying only `set` makes
# REQ-0009 exit 3, because REQ-0009 refines REQ-0008 and REQ-0008 is then undecided.
corpus_set=parity_and_adversarial set=direction_gold_structural runs=25 deployment_mode=air_gapped field=value
corpus_set=parity set=direction_gold_structural runs=25 deployment_mode=air_gapped field=value
